# Page metadata and history

Show when guidance was published, what changed and when it last changed.

## Own editorial dates without inventing freshness

This page owns publication and update-history presentation. The [review workflow](../patterns/review-dates.html) owns what an actual review checks and when another is due. The [withdrawn NHS review-date source page](review-date.html) stays available for provenance; it is not a separate component to reinstate.

Keep first publication, substantive update, complete editorial review and planned review as separately named facts. Preserve an overdue review date until review occurs. Device observation times belong to [data guidance](../content/numbers-and-data.html), not editorial history. Neither a successful build nor a page render may silently replace any of these dates.

## When to use

Every editorial guidance page in this design system has publication metadata and an expandable update history. The homepage is excluded. Standalone example canvases are linked demonstrations; their owning guidance page records their changes.

Do not confuse publication dates with a sensor timestamp, a household event log or a review deadline. Use the [review-dates pattern](../patterns/review-dates.html) for planned content review and native HA history for device events.

